* "German Quad", channel 3: V1A, GAIN 3 and the common tube Tc, V2A and the V2B follower, the CH3 tone stack and VOLUME 3. See preamp.net for the drawing and the assumptions.

V VRAIL x 100 400
R R86 x dp 18.5k
C C87 dp 0 8.4u
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* V1A: 1M and 100p to ground, the 68k stopper (the input capacitor is bridged on the drawing), 1k2 with 10u on the cathode, 120k plate load.
R R1M in 0 1M
C C100P in 0 100p
R R68K in g1 68k
T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R1K2 k1 0 1.2k
C C10U k1 0 10u
R R120A dp p1 120k

* CH3: 1n and 220k from V1A's plate into GAIN 3 (220k-A wiper pot), 220k at its wiper, which ST3 brings to the grid gt of the common tube Tc (1M to ground).
C C1N3 p1 q3 1n
R R220C q3 s3 220k
R VRG_T s3 w3 1
R VRG_B w3 0 1
R R220G w3 0 220k
R RST3 w3 gt 1

* The load of the next stage at gt (Tc's 1M grid resistor and its Miller input capacitance), repeated here so the cut keeps it; the rail resistor above is
* scaled by (the channel's current / this stage's current) so the plates sit where they did in one netlist.
R RDUM gt 0 1M
C CMIL gt 0 88p
